# The line endings this repository actually uses, written down so a checkout on
# another machine cannot quietly rewrite them.
#
# `tools/check_docs.py` fails on any CR byte in a `.md` (a stray \r renders as a
# visible box in the middle of a Chinese paragraph), and the `.bat` files are CRLF
# by construction - `cmd.exe` is unreliable with LF batch files. Without this file
# a Windows checkout with the usual `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every LF to CRLF
# and `python tools/check_docs.py` starts failing on files nobody edited.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binaries (the DLLs, the PGMs, the build trees)
# and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Last match wins, so these two override the line above.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
